Cross-Border Transfer Assessment with SCCs
Objectives
By completing this lab, you will:

Model a UAE-to-EU HR data transfer flow and classify data categories by sensitivity
Apply GDPR Chapter V adequacy logic and determine applicable transfer mechanisms
Populate an SCC Module (Controller-to-Processor) and a supplementary measures checklist
Produce a Transfer Impact Assessment (TIA) in Markdown with a risk-based recommendation
Evaluate technical mitigations (encryption-in-transit, tokenization, localization) against residual risk
Prerequisites
Working knowledge of GDPR Articles 44-49, EU SCCs (2021/914), and KSA PDPL cross-border provisions
Familiarity with data flow diagramming and risk scoring methodologies
Comfort with Git, Markdown, YAML/JSON, and CLI-based Linux tools
No prior use of a specific transfer-assessment tool required — you will assemble the workflow yourself
Environment Setup
Single Linux machine (provided via Start Lab). Install lightweight open-source tooling:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y git jq python3-pip graphviz
pip3 install pyyaml
mkdir -p ~/tia-lab/{data,diagrams,assessment}
cd ~/tia-lab
git init
Download reference dataset (sample HR fields) — create it yourself as instructed in Task 1.

